{"id":"h010","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? Mars has no natural moons.","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"Mars's moons are very small, irregular, and hard to see from the surface.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Because the moons are small and hard to see, the idea that Mars has none is not an absurd guess.","confidence":0.7,"lean":1,"theta":1.0996,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"Neither moon is large enough to be a major feature of Mars's sky like Earth's Moon.","confidence":0.85,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.3352,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Size and visibility considerations do not support the claim that Mars has no moons.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Mars has two natural satellites, Phobos and Deimos.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Asaph Hall discovered both moons in 1877.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Phobos is about 22 km across and Deimos about 12 km.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Both moons have been imaged by spacecraft and their orbits are well measured.","confidence":0.92,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4451,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Direct observational evidence of two moons is decisive, and small size does not change that they exist.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The claim that Mars has no natural moons is false.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":9,"J":-0.7,"relation":"contradic